# Never hoist React's type packages.
#
# The web app is on React 19 and the Expo app is on React 18, which is correct
# for each. pnpm gives every package its own copy, but it also builds a hidden
# fallback directory at node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules and hoists one version
# of each package into it. Once the mobile app existed, the version that landed
# there was @types/react@18.
#
# Next.js's own .d.ts files import "react" from deep inside .pnpm/, so they walk
# up and hit that hoisted copy — while apps/web resolves its own @types/react@19
# normally. One compilation, two React type identities, and every JSX element in
# the web app fails with "ReactNode is not assignable to ReactNode".
#
# Excluding the two type packages from hoisting means nothing can resolve them
# by accident; each app only ever sees the copy in its own node_modules.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
